circuit-trace 1
# Skeleton: pairs of diodes become due on the same tick, scheduled in an order
# that differs from the expected priority order. Row z=0: a repeater feeding a
# repeater against one feeding a lamp. Rows z=3/-3: a repeater turning off
# against one turning on. Row z=6: comparators feeding a repeater or a lamp.
# Row z=-6: a repeater whose front diode faces back into it. Rows z=9/12: a
# pulse-extended repeater feeding a repeater against a repeater turning off.
title Scheduled-tick priorities of repeaters and comparators
game-version 1.21.8
source circuit_reference
harness -
mechanisms scheduled_ticks repeater comparator
